# BATCH FILES ARE CRLF, AND THIS IS NOT COSMETIC.
#
# cmd.exe resumes a running batch file by BYTE OFFSET. With LF-only line
# endings that arithmetic drifts, and a large file jumps: run-phase.bat with
# LF was measured on 2026-08-31 leaving the reload check and arriving at
# :noadvances - refusing a unit for a missing ADVANCES field that no arbiter
# had yet been asked for - and, in another layout, failing to find :budget,
# a label that is plainly in the file. The same file converted to CRLF, in
# the same directory against the same root, took the correct branch.
#
# It is the same mechanism PHASE_PLAN.md's ruling of 2026-08-31 already
# records for a file edited while it runs. This entry stops it arriving from
# the other side: a session writing a .bat with LF endings.
#
# The working copies in this tree were LF because sessions wrote them that
# way; git's own blobs are LF and core.autocrlf was already converting on
# checkout. This makes the checkout rule explicit rather than dependent on
# one machine's setting.
*.bat text eol=crlf
